## 🐧 1. Linux Command Line Revision

Revised the following Linux commands:

| Command     | Purpose                                 |
| ----------- | --------------------------------------- |
| `cat`       | Display file contents                   |
| `cat -n`    | Display file contents with line numbers |
| `head`      | Display the beginning of a file         |
| `head -n 1` | Display the first line of a file        |
| `head -c 1` | Display the first byte of a file        |
| `tail`      | Display the end of a file               |
| `tail -n 1` | Display the last line of a file         |
| `tail -c 1` | Display the last byte of a file         |
| `tail -c 2` | Display the last two bytes of a file    |
| `diff`      | Compare two files                       |
| `diff -r`   | Compare directories recursively         |

**Key Learning:** These commands are useful for file inspection, comparing data, troubleshooting, and analyzing files during Linux administration and cybersecurity investigations.

